WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.666 --> 00:00:04.700
Be careful.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.633
Amazing.

00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:11.733
It moves!

00:00:13.266 --> 00:00:17.000
The direction is done based on

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.766
the drawings and timesheet done by the animators.

00:00:23.766 --> 00:00:28.700
Like, we want this scene or this cut to have a certain atmosphere,

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.900
and we give instructions and direct it.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.733
Based on the instructions,

00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:37.433
the Chief Animation Director, that is,

00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:44.766
the person who directs the movement of the character in the drawing,

00:00:44.766 --> 00:00:47.233
will do the correction.

00:00:47.233 --> 00:00:50.200
In some cases, we'll do a retake,

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.066
and ask the animator in charge, who drew the picture, to draw it again.

00:00:55.066 --> 00:01:01.800
After that, depending on the anime or the workplace,

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.266
the Chief Animation Producer,

00:01:04.266 --> 00:01:05.766
which is me in this case,

00:01:05.766 --> 00:01:10.933
will check for consistency of characters,

00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:15.066
like the facial expression, which must be consistent.

00:01:15.066 --> 00:01:18.466
I also give them suggestions on how to draw something,

00:01:18.466 --> 00:01:24.733
and I would draw it out and make corrections.

00:01:24.733 --> 00:01:30.866
The above has been the work process of layout and rough draft.

00:01:30.866 --> 00:01:36.466
After this, the drawings with added corrections

00:01:36.466 --> 00:01:43.933
are returned to the animator in charge, who drew the layout.

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:49.233
The contents that have been corrected will be reflected,

00:01:49.233 --> 00:01:56.466
and it'll be made into a clear copy, like a proper,

00:01:56.466 --> 00:01:58.800
clean drawing copy.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.066
It's the work process of the key animation.

00:02:01.066 --> 00:02:04.600
When we draw a person punching someone in the key animation,

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.633
for example, we have the drawing of his arm pulled back,

00:02:08.633 --> 00:02:12.133
this drawing of him starting to jab,

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:15.866
and the drawing with the arm extended, which are included in our key animation.

00:02:15.866 --> 00:02:19.033
If it's only these three, it'd really be…

00:02:19.866 --> 00:02:21.766
It would go quickly,

00:02:21.766 --> 00:02:26.733
or the movement will become stiff with pauses like this,

00:02:26.733 --> 00:02:28.500
so we need drawings in between.

00:02:29.466 --> 00:02:33.133
The instruction is made into timesheets.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:39.433
We must fill in the blanks between clean copies of key animation drawings,

00:02:40.233 --> 00:02:44.333
done by adding drawings in between. That's the process of animation.

00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:49.366
By the way, the number of pages of this animation drawings is 22.

00:02:49.366 --> 00:02:51.733
We have 17 pages of key animation drawings.

00:02:51.733 --> 00:02:56.600
We've added drawings in between in the animation and made it into 22 pages.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:00.433
So five pages were inserted in between in the animation.

00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:06.233
After this process, we check it on an actual screen all together.

00:03:06.233 --> 00:03:10.233
If we get an okay, then the process of this cut is complete.

00:03:10.233 --> 00:03:13.833
This is the timesheet and the key animation.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.100
You'll wonder what it is, if it's just this.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.066
This is also a rough draft.

00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:32.500
It's drawn quite roughly.

00:03:34.166 --> 00:03:35.800
This will do.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:45.600
Camera work is added and it's filmed as a trial run.

00:03:51.366 --> 00:03:52.833
This is the key animation.

00:03:57.233 --> 00:03:59.133
It's the background art.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.466
Combining them, it becomes like this.

00:04:04.466 --> 00:04:06.533
This is only in an instant, too.

00:04:06.533 --> 00:04:08.633
There's a lot in the filming part already.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:20.400
So it's seven and a third.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.800
Each character is different,

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:30.866
but it's basically about 3.5 till it reaches his crotch.

00:04:30.866 --> 00:04:33.266
That's where the crotch is.

00:04:33.266 --> 00:04:36.566
The upper body is about 3.5 heads long.

00:04:36.566 --> 00:04:39.800
It's a bit late to say this,

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:45.000
but this is used as a rough guide.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.966
Especially when we draw it this time,

00:04:48.966 --> 00:04:55.500
we aren't drawing it as a job of a pro animator,

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.066
so I don't think we need to match it so strictly.

00:04:59.066 --> 00:05:07.033
This is the protagonist, a character called Edamame, who is a swindler.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:11.400
He can't fight, and he is weak,

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:16.000
so he is thin and has a slender figure.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.133
He has sloping shoulders, and his shoulders are narrow.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:24.166
This is Edamame's characteristic.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.166
It's very important.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.900
In terms of figure, she's slim.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.533
All the characters we've seen are slim.

00:05:32.533 --> 00:05:36.466
They're Yoshiyuki Sadamoto-san's characters,

00:05:36.466 --> 00:05:40.566
so they're all slim, like Evangelions.

